<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
    
    <!-- NuGet Package Metadata -->
    <Title>EffinitiveFramework.Core</Title>
    <Authors>Henry Bartosch</Authors>
    <PackageId>EffinitiveFramework.Core</PackageId>
    <Version>2.8.0</Version>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/HBartosch/Effinitive</RepositoryUrl>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/HBartosch/Effinitive</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PackageTags>http;http2;web-framework;high-performance;zero-allocation;minimal-api;aspnetcore-alternative;hpack;alpn;tls;https;fast;low-latency;microservices;sse;server-sent-events;streaming</PackageTags>
    <Description>HTTP/1.1, HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 web framework for .NET 8+, built from scratch. Allocation-conscious routing, a custom HTTP/2 implementation with HPACK, WebSockets, TLS with per-listener ALPN and certificate rotation, response caching, rate limiting and OpenAPI generation.</Description>
    <PackageIcon>PackageIconResized.png</PackageIcon>
    <PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE</PackageLicenseFile>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>v2.8.0: a request no longer crosses a thread twice before it is parsed, and a WebSocket connection no longer shares the server's cancellation source.

Fixed. A WebSocket handler was given the server-wide shutdown token and passes it to a pipe read on every message. A suspended read registers a callback against the source behind its token, so every connection on every core registered against one registration list and its lock landed on the path each message follows. The cost grew with core count rather than with the work. Each connection now gets a source linked to the server's, so a stop still releases a handler parked on a read. Per-message processor time 26.3 to 16.3 microseconds, p99 6.56 to 3.31ms, and the cost no longer rises with core count.

Changed. The receive completed on an I/O queue and the pipe then handed its reader continuation to the thread pool; the second crossing bought nothing. The receive now completes on the pool and the reader runs on that same thread. At 4096 connections: 463,221 to 732,706 requests per second, 37.95 to 24.43 microseconds of processor time per request, p99 41.70 to 17.40ms. The handler runs on a pool thread either way, so a handler that blocks costs the same resource as before. Set ServerOptions.InlineRequestProcessing to false to restore the previous path.

Changed. Request bodies and query strings no longer allocate a copy: a deferred body is drained into a pooled buffer rather than a MemoryStream and a ToArray, and a query holds offsets into the path rather than a dictionary of strings. 3,450 to 1,352 bytes allocated per request. A plus in a query is still left as itself, per RFC 3986 section 3.4.

Measured on a 20 core host rather than the public board's hardware. Arena validation passes 112 checks with none failing, and the WebSocket suite reports the same 301 cases as 2.7.1 with no failures.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2025 Henry Bartosch</Copyright>
    <PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>false</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>false</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="EffinitiveFramework.Tests" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="EffinitiveFramework.Benchmarks" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- HTTP/3 (QUIC) only available on .NET 10+ -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net8.0'">
    <Compile Remove="Http3\**" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.NetAnalyzers" Version="9.0.0" Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net8.0'">
      <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
    </PackageReference>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.NetAnalyzers" Version="10.0.100" Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net10.0'">
      <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
    </PackageReference>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.ObjectPool" Version="8.0.0" Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net8.0'" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.ObjectPool" Version="10.0.0" Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net10.0'" />
    <PackageReference Include="SecurityCodeScan.VS2019" Version="5.6.7">
      <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
    </PackageReference>
    <PackageReference Include="System.IO.Pipelines" Version="8.0.0" Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net8.0'" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.IO.Pipelines" Version="10.0.0" Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net10.0'" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.IdentityModel.Tokens.Jwt" Version="8.16.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Routya.ResultKit" Version="2.1.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\LICENSE" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\..\PackageIconResized.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
